    'cal.white': 'All your lights are white now. If this one looks bluer or more yellow than the rest, move the slider until it matches them.',
    'dev.check': 'Check connection', 'path.hint': 'Also seen through OpenRGB as {0}: which way lights it is chosen on that card', 'path.st.orgb': 'Lit through OpenRGB, as {0}', 'path.st.direct': 'Lit directly, as {0}', 'path.note': 'haku may see one device twice: through its own driver and through OpenRGB. Say so here, and only one of them lights it: the other lets go first. haku only guesses the pair from the maker\'s name, so check it is the same device.', 'path.own': '{0}: left to its own program', 'path.orgb': '{0}: haku lights it through OpenRGB', 'path.direct': '{0}: haku lights it directly', 'path.none': 'None: a device of its own', 'path.title': 'Same device as', 'dev.waits': 'haku tries again less often, up to once a minute', 'dev.retry.t': 'Try to connect again now: the devices not connected start over from short waits', 'dev.retry': 'Retry now', 'chk.busy': 'Checking… (a few seconds)', 'chk.ok': 'All good: it answers and takes the colours.',
    'chk.answers': '{0} is on the network but doesn\'t take haku\'s connection. Turn on local (LAN) control in its own app, or close another program that holds it.',
    'chk.silent': 'No answer from {0}. It\'s unplugged or switched off at the wall, has dropped off the Wi‑Fi, or the router gave it a new address. Search for devices to find it again.',
    'chk.subnet': 'This PC isn\'t on the network of {0}. Connect the PC to the same router or Wi‑Fi (not a guest network or a VPN).',
    'chk.name': 'Reconnecting didn\'t help. This device isn\'t reached over the local network: check its cable or its account.',
    'dev.hint.wled': 'WLED controller: its IP address (port 80). Frames go over UDP realtime (port 21324).',
    'dev.hint.openrgb': 'OpenRGB with the SDK server on (default 127.0.0.1, port 6742). Controller # is its position in OpenRGB\'s device list, from 0.',
    'dev.hint.govee': 'Turn on "LAN Control" for the light in the Govee Home app first. No such switch (e.g. AI Sync Box 2)? Use Govee (cloud) under Sign-ins.',
    'dev.hint.goveecloud': 'Connect your Govee API key under Sign-ins first; then Find devices lists the account\'s devices.',
    'dev.hint.nlusb': 'Found on USB by Find devices (quit Nanoleaf Desktop first).',
    'dev.hint.nanoleaf': 'IP address of the controller or strip (see your router, or the Nanoleaf app). After Add, allow the connection: hold the controller power button 5–7 s, or for MAGRGB / Essentials press Connect to API in the device settings of the Nanoleaf app, within 90 s.',
    'dev.hint.lifx': 'LIFX bulb or strip: its IP address.',
    'dev.hint.wiz': 'WiZ bulb or strip: its IP address. No app setting needed.',
    'dev.hint.divoom': 'Divoom Times Gate: its IP address (the Divoom app shows it under the device\'s settings). Then enter its LocalToken on the device card. Its lights (behind the screens and along the edge) follow the effect; the screens keep showing what you set in the Divoom app. Experimental.',
    'dv.token': 'The number from the Divoom app: the device → settings → LocalToken. Without it the device takes no commands.',
    'dev.hint.wooting': 'Wooting keyboard on USB: found by Find devices. Effects run across it from left to right; when haku control lets go, the keyboard gets its own lighting back. Its lighting has to be on (brightness above zero).',
    'dev.hint.razer': 'Razer devices through Razer Synapse, which has to run. While Synapse answers, Find devices offers each kind of Razer device (keyboard, mouse, mousepad, headset, keypad, Chroma Link): add the ones you have. Keyboards show the effects from left to right, mice from front to back. When haku control lets go, Synapse shows its own lighting again.',
    'dev.hint.steelseries': 'SteelSeries devices through SteelSeries GG, which has to run. Find devices offers the keyboard and the other devices (mice, headsets, mousepads): add the ones you have. When haku control lets go, GG shows its own lighting again.',
    'dev.hint.logitech': 'Logitech devices through Logitech G HUB, which has to run (with "Allow games & applications to control my lighting" on). Find devices offers the keyboard and the other lights (mice, headsets, speakers: one colour): add the ones you have. When haku control lets go, G HUB shows its own lighting again.',
    'dev.hint.aura': 'The ASUS board’s own LEDs (the ROG logo, the I/O cover) over its USB Aura controller: found by Find devices. Close Armoury Crate (LightingService) first. The ARGB headers stay with OpenRGB. If the board does not say how many LEDs it has, Calibrate finds the count.',
    'dev.hint.lianli': 'A Lian Li wireless fan group (SL, TL, SL-INF, CL, P28) over the radio: found by Find devices once the Fans page hears it on this PC’s dongle. The LED count comes with the fan model. Close L-Connect first; a group that follows the board’s ARGB is taken off it while haku lights it.',
    'dev.hint.tryx': 'TRYX PANORAMA cooler’s screen on USB: found by Find devices (quit TRYX KANALI first, it holds the port).', 'tx.busy': 'the port is held by another program', 'tx.theme': 'Screen theme', 'tx.keep': 'As TRYX KANALI left it', 'tx.follow': 'Screen off with the lights, brightness with haku’s', 'tx.note': 'The themes are the PANORAMA’s own (the 240 SE may have others). Your own picture, GIF or mp4 (up to 16 MB) goes over the cable at about 40–70 KB/s: 2 MB take under a minute, and it is sent once. GIFs may not play on the 240 SE. The cooler’s LEDs are on the motherboard’s ARGB header.', 'tx.build': 'Make one…', 'txb.title': 'Screen builder · {0}', 'txb.src': 'Picture, GIF or video…', 'txb.shape': 'Screen shape', 'txb.zoom': 'Zoom', 'txb.stage': 'Preview: drag to move the picture or the chosen text, the wheel zooms, arrow keys move too',
    'txb.note': 'Drag the picture to choose what shows; the wheel or Zoom comes closer. Texts and pictures over it move the same way, or with the arrow keys. A GIF or video becomes an mp4 of up to 30 s, made as it plays; a still becomes a JPEG. What you add is part of the file: live figures such as temperatures are not shown yet.',
